&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly technical, execution-focused &lt;strong&gt;Cloud Backend Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to serve as the technical lead for our core cloud engineering pod. In this role, you will drive technical excellence through active, hands-on implementation and maintain deep module-level ownership of core system components.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will participate in the technical roadmap definition, own the end-to-end execution of major platform components, and lead a talented team designing the server-side backend architectures that power next-generation software-defined vehicle platforms. You will be responsible for building the scalable, high-throughput cloud networks that interface directly with physical edge hardware, processing complex vehicle datasets from distributed fleets globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Implementation &amp;amp; Module Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively write core, high-performance Go/cloud infrastructure code while maintaining direct ownership over the architecture, quality, and technical health of critical backend modules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logger &amp;amp; Ingestion Pipeline Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and optimise highly resilient, distributed cloud-native ingestion services capable of parsing, sorting, and processing massive binary or structured data payloads streaming from vehicle edge data loggers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote Fleet Command &amp;amp; Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect the configuration and orchestration APIs used to safely push configuration scripts, remote triggers, and firmware updates downward to vehicle loggers under constrained or intermittent cellular network conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Evolution &amp;amp; AI Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Scale, recruit, mentor, and grow a highly technical AI backend engineering team responsible for core AI development, automation loops, and platform integrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Database &amp;amp; Storage Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement storage-tiering architectures (SQL, NoSQL, and OLAP databases) designed to transition data pipelines from real-time streaming alerts into cold-storage data lakes efficiently and cost-effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Mentorship &amp;amp; Code Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive technical excellence across the pod by establishing rigorous code reviews, automated CI/CD pipelines, and robust service testing guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Alignment &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver major platform components on schedule, acting as a definitive technical authority for your backend pod who translates system requirements into concrete deliverables for product managers, front-end developers, and international engineering hubs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 9+ years of backend software development experience, with a proven track record of leading technical engineering squads as a Tech Lead, Component Owner, or Engineering Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logger System Domain Familiarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong experience interacting with or building the cloud/server-side components of hardware data logger ecosystems (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Intrepid Control Systems’ Wireless neoVI, neoVI Plasma&lt;/strong&gt;, Vector data logging servers, or equivalent industrial IoT/automotive edge-to-cloud architectures).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Telemetry Data Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Conceptual or practical understanding of processing vehicle bus protocols (CAN, LIN, Automotive Ethernet) and their associated log file representations (e.g., BLF, MDF4, PCAP) at the cloud ingestion layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Implementation:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of successful development of an AI/ML feature, intelligent workflow, or model pipeline delivered into a production distributed cloud environment.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud &amp;amp; Infrastructure Stack:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency with public cloud platforms, utilizing microservices, serverless solutions, containerization (&lt;strong&gt;Docker&lt;/strong&gt;), and orchestrators (&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;Go (strongly preferred)&lt;/strong&gt; or other low-latency systems-level back-end languages (e.g., Rust, Java, C++).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed Processing:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience scaling real-time distributed message fabrics and streaming compute engines (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Kafka&lt;/strong&gt;, RabbitMQ, Spark Pipelines).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decisive Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional communication and problem-solving skills; a technical leader who can drive the engineering execution of complex modules while collaborating across global time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ireland Office Benefits &amp;amp; Perks Offered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off (national holidays and statutory annual leave provisions apply)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical and Dental Insurance (for you and your dependents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Income protection and Life insurance benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occupational Pension Plan - Sonatus match up to 5% of your contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefit allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phone &amp;amp; internet reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Accessory Allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily Deliveroo Lunch Credit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid office work-arrangement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Senior Cloud Platform Engineer to own the cloud infrastructure and delivery pipeline supporting one of our largest OEM programs. This role is based on-site at the customer&#39;s engineering facility, embedded alongside their teams. You will build and operate our GCP-based platform using GitOps and infrastructure-as-code, automate the paths that get software from commit to production, and act as the local owner for cloud access, environment provisioning, and day-to-day operational issues. This is a hands-on role for a broad, self-directed engineer who is comfortable being the on-site technical point of contact and working across organizational boundaries to unblock delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roles and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve our GCP cloud platform for the program - GKE, IAM, Vertex, networking, and supporting services - with a focus on reliability, security, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain infrastructure as code in Terraform, treating all environment configuration as reviewed, versioned, and reproducible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate the platform using GitOps practices (Argo CD, Helm), so that environment state is declarative and every change is traceable to a commit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain CI/CD automation that takes services from commit to deployment with minimal manual intervention, including progressive delivery patterns such as blue/green and canary rollouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build observability and alerting that gives both Sonatus and the customer a clear view of system health, and lead troubleshooting when things break.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the on-site owner for cloud access and environment issues - coordinating permissions, provisioning, and workflow questions directly with the customer&#39;s IT and platform teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the program&#39;s AI resources - model access, GPU and accelerator capacity, quotas, and API keys across Vertex and other model services - and track usage and spend so teams get the capacity they need within budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize AI model deployment and serving for latency, throughput, and cost, including model selection, right-sizing, batching, caching, and quantization, and measure the results against agreed benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate recurring operational work and reduce toil, so that developer velocity does not depend on manual intervention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sonatus engineering teams in California, Ireland, Korea, and India to keep the on-site environment aligned with our broader platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience building and operating production cloud infrastructure, with a strong DevOps, platform engineering, or SRE background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on experience with Google Cloud Platform (GKE, IAM, VPC/networking, Cloud Build, or equivalent). Experience with AWS or Azure is welcome, but GCP depth is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Terraform skills and a track record of managing real production infrastructure as code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with GitOps workflows and tooling (Argo CD, Flux, Helm) and a preference for declarative, version-controlled operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid Kubernetes and containerization experience - deploying, scaling, securing, and debugging real workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong automation and scripting ability (Python, Go, or Bash) and a bias toward eliminating manual steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Jenkins, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating independently in a customer environment: strong communication, sound judgment on what to escalate, and the credibility to work directly with a partner organization&#39;s engineering and IT teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ML or AI workloads running on cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working embedded at, or delivering into, a large enterprise or automotive customer environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud cost management and FinOps practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security and compliance experience in a regulated or enterprise setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks Offered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health care plan (Medical, Dental &amp;amp; Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and Dependent Care Expense program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement plan (401k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Insurance (Basic, Voluntary &amp;amp; AD&amp;amp;D)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid time off per year, 14+ paid holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefit allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phone &amp;amp; Internet reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Accessory Allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The posted salary range is a general guideline and represents a good faith estimate of what Sonatus (&quot;Company&quot;) could reasonably expect to pay for a base salary for this position. The pay offered to a selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, geographic location and external market pay for comparable jobs. The Company reserves the right to modify this range in the future, as needed, as market conditions change.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$137,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sonatus, we are building the &quot;Fastest yet Safest&quot; software for the Software-Defined Vehicle (SDV) era. As we accelerate innovation, maintaining the highest standards of safety and security is paramount.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Compliance Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to oversee our engineering compliance and quality strategy. You will play a pivotal role in balancing agile execution with automotive rigor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this position, you will join the &lt;strong&gt;Compliance Squad&lt;/strong&gt;, serving as a key contributor of &lt;strong&gt;A-SPICE, Cybersecurity (ISO 21434), and Process Quality&lt;/strong&gt;. You will collaborate with the team to help maintain quality gates for product releases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Release Gatekeeping &amp;amp; Quality Approval&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in maintaining quality gates for software releases. You participate in the strategy to approve product deployment based on objective quality criteria and compliance readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review validation results from the release pipeline and external partners to ensure &quot;Production-Ready&quot; standards are met before final delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Process Optimization &amp;amp; Cybersecurity Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and follow a &quot;Lightweight yet Compliant&quot; engineering process based on &lt;strong&gt;A-SPICE&lt;/strong&gt;, integrated seamlessly into Jira/Confluence/Jama workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cybersecurity:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the execution of ISO 21434 compliance tasks. Conduct Threat Analysis and Risk Assessment (TARA), OSS CVE and ensure security controls are properly implemented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Code Quality &amp;amp; Static Analysis Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the delivery of official static analysis reports to OEM customers, covering &lt;strong&gt;MISRA C++, RTE, CERT C++, and HIS Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Issue Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Prioritize code quality violations and collaborate with Engineering Squads to track &quot;Must-Fix&quot; issues to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Defense:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the technical justification process for rule deviations and handle customer inquiries regarding code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Audit Defense&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support for external audits and compliance assessments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Essential Background]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;: B.S. or higher in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 3–7 years of experience in Automotive Software Quality or Systems Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Core Competencies]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Knowledge: &lt;/strong&gt;Expert-level understanding of &lt;strong&gt;Automotive SPICE (ASPICE)&lt;/strong&gt; AND/OR &lt;strong&gt;ISO 21434 (Cybersecurity)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Static Analysis Mastery&lt;/strong&gt;: Proficiency in managing code quality standards (&lt;strong&gt;MISRA C/C++, RTE, CERT C++&lt;/strong&gt;) using tools like &lt;strong&gt;Coverity, Polyspace, or QAC&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;: Hands-on experience with &lt;strong&gt;Automotive SPICE (ASPICE)&lt;/strong&gt; assessment and process definition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: Hands-on experience supporting or defending external audits, including preparing evidence and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;: Proven ability to work effectively within cross-functional engineering teams to drive quality and compliance outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Knowledge and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Certifications &amp;amp; Tools]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt; Certified Functional Safety Expert/Professional (CFSE/CFSP), Cybersecurity certification (CACSP), or ASPICE Assessor qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Toolchain:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;Jira/Confluence&lt;/strong&gt; for process management and Requirements Management tools (Jama, CodeBeamer).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Soft Skills &amp;amp; Bonus]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience as a software developer or architect is a strong plus. Specifically:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Dependencies:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with build systems like Yocto (Bitbake) or CMake to configure static analysis captures and accurately trace OSS dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kernel &amp;amp; OS Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with Linux Kernel configuration (Kconfig) and security hardening (e.g., SELinux, Secure Boot) to validate OS-level compliance strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of HW/SW interfaces (MMU, Hypervisors) to assess Freedom From Interference (FFI) mechanisms for Functional Safety concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in English (Written &amp;amp; Verbal) to communicate with HQ and global OEM customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to build and optimize processes in a fast-paced, growth-oriented environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits Offered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and equity program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support 4 social insurance plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family leave (Maternity, Paternity)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid office work-arrangement/flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perk Offerings:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complimentary lunch/dinner, snacks and beverages during on-site working days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefit allowances (towards gym membership and fitness programs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phone &amp;amp; Internet reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Accessory Allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Appreciation Gift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Health Checkup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support English class&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Engagement Offerings:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Departmental team building and outings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Referral Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture/Employee Satisfaction Surveys - Feedback matters!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovative Award Program (annual)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sonatus is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California with international locations in Ireland, France, Germany, Poland, Korea, China, India, Taiwan and Japan. This is a hybrid position at our Pangyo location. You will report to the Engineering Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sonatus is bringing production-grade AI to the vehicle edge with &lt;strong&gt;Fastlane™ Edge&lt;/strong&gt;, the in-vehicle AI runtime that lets OEMs deploy, run, monitor and update AI models, virtual sensors and diagnostic logic on existing vehicle computers. Our Customer Success organization operates as &lt;strong&gt;Mission-Driven Squads&lt;/strong&gt; that take full end-to-end ownership of a module, from implementation to verification to on-site support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Embedded AI Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Korea Customer Success team and put edge AI into our Korean OEM programs. You will bring up the Fastlane Edge runtime on customer hardware, onboard AI models authored by partners, by the customer and by Sonatus, help customer engineers author their own models with the Sonatus SDK, validate models on real vehicles, and tune Sonatus in-house virtual-sensor models on customer data using our MLOps toolchain. You will act as a technical contact for the customer on edge AI integration topics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for an engineer who is comfortable in a Python training pipeline, inside a Linux container on an automotive ECU, and in a vehicle at a customer test site. Model development is part of the job, but always in service of a customer deliverable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Edge AI Runtime Integration on Customer Hardware&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Bring-Up&lt;/strong&gt;: Bring up and maintain Fastlane Edge on customer targets — Sonatus gateway units (Fastlane Copilot) and customer control units — including CAN/CAN-FD bring-up, DBC/ARXML integration, sandbox and Python-runtime deployment, security-policy adjustments and cloud connectivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SDK Integration&lt;/strong&gt;: Integrate the runtime with customer platforms via the Sonatus Southbound SDK where direct bus access is not available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runbook Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;: Maintain the Korea integration runbooks and default configurations; work with the platform team to turn one-off demo fixes into mergeable, released code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. AI Model Onboarding and Validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model Packaging&lt;/strong&gt;: Validate, package and deploy AI model bundles from partners, from customer engineers and from Sonatus using the Sonatus ADK: input-signal mapping, sampling and output schema review, dependency checks, resource budgets and OTA deployment through the Sonatus Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Concurrency Verification&lt;/strong&gt;: Verify multi-model concurrency on a single ECU within agreed CPU/RAM envelopes; measure and document per-model resource profiles and telemetry policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Native Porting &amp;amp; Optimization&lt;/strong&gt;: Migrate Python-developed models to production-ready native (C++/ONNX Runtime) bundles, including model conversion, native integration and optimization, with automated numerical-parity validation against reference implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Customer Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training &amp;amp; Office Hours&lt;/strong&gt;: Deliver SDK/ADK training and office hours in Korean for customer engineers authoring their own models; support model-contract (config.yml) authoring and signal-to-input mapping from customer network databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements Capture&lt;/strong&gt;: Help capture customer AI workload requirements (use case, signals, rates, accuracy/latency targets, resource and data-sovereignty constraints) and document them for Sonatus product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation as Code&lt;/strong&gt;: Treat documentation as code: integration guides, troubleshooting FAQs and release notes in Korean and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Model Development and Tuning on Customer Data&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLOps Toolchain&lt;/strong&gt;: Run customer vehicle captures through the Sonatus MLOps toolchain: data ingest and alignment, recipe-driven training, model-family A/B comparison (gradient boosting, temporal convolutional and physics-informed models), ONNX export, quantization and on-target latency measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Virtual-Sensor Tuning&lt;/strong&gt;: Tune Sonatus virtual-sensor and estimation models on customer drives and deliver them as validated bundles with customer-facing reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ground Truth &amp;amp; Datasets&lt;/strong&gt;: Define ground-truth capture (reference sensors, co-logging) and dataset versioning; contribute fixes and hardening upstream to the toolchain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. On-Vehicle Validation, Demos and Customer Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Validation Drives&lt;/strong&gt;: Execute on-vehicle validation and comparison drives; contribute to acceptance criteria and shadow-mode protocols with the customer and Sonatus QA; produce traceable test evidence and, where required, ASPICE v4 MLE artifacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Site Support&lt;/strong&gt;: Support major test events and demos on-site, troubleshooting integration issues directly in the vehicle or on the bench.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Defect Triage&lt;/strong&gt;: Act as a technical contact for edge AI integration issues; reproduce, isolate (bundle vs. runtime vs. cloud), and follow customer-found defects through the Sonatus release train.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. AI-Augmented Workflow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;: Leverage AI tools such as Claude and GitHub Copilot to accelerate recipe authoring, test generation, log analysis and documentation, within customer data-governance constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Essential Background]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical/Control Engineering or a related field; Master’s degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 5+ years of experience in machine learning engineering or embedded software, including 2+ years deploying ML models on edge or embedded Linux targets. Customer-facing integration, field application or solutions engineering experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages &amp;amp; Systems&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong Python; ability to read, build and debug modern C++ (C++14/17); solid Linux debugging skills (systemd, processes and logs, containers; exposure to cgroups, sandboxing, seccomp or shared-library/glibc issues is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Core Competencies]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Device/Signal Data&lt;/strong&gt;: Hands-on experience working with structured device or bus-level signal data — automotive (CAN/CAN-FD), industrial fieldbus, or similar — including signal mapping, sampling and time alignment. Familiarity with automotive-specific protocols (DBC/ARXML, UDS, SOME/IP, DLT) is a plus, not a prerequisite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ML Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;: ML deployment experience with ONNX/ONNX Runtime and PyTorch or scikit-learn/XGBoost; exposure to quantization and latency/memory profiling on ARM (aarch64) targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applied Modeling&lt;/strong&gt;: Applied modeling experience with time-series or vehicle-signal data (regression, estimation or anomaly detection) and the ability to evaluate models against agreed metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ML Pipelines &amp;amp; Data Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;: Experience with reproducible ML pipelines and data tooling such as Parquet, Apache Arrow or DuckDB, experiment tracking and versioned datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verification Mindset&lt;/strong&gt;: Python test automation and evidence-based triage; willingness to split time between development and validation as the mission requires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication&lt;/strong&gt;: Fluent Korean and professional English; clear technical writing and comfort supporting customer engineers and on-site test events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;: Results-driven, with strong problem-solving skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with customer and internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Knowledge and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: Hands-on experience with NXP S32 family / eIQ Auto, Qualcomm SA8xxx / SNPE-QNN, or comparable embedded compute platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vehicle Dynamics&lt;/strong&gt;: Vehicle dynamics, chassis or body control-domain knowledge; prior virtual-sensor or sensor-replacement work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OEM IT &amp;amp; Security Stacks&lt;/strong&gt;: Familiarity with OEM IT and security stacks (Kubernetes, Harbor/Nexus, Kafka, SonarQube/Blackduck, security review processes) and data-sovereignty requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards Awareness&lt;/strong&gt;: Awareness of ASPICE v4 (Machine Learning Engineering process group), ISO 26262 and ISO 21448 as applied to ML components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LLM-Assisted Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;: Experience with LLM-assisted engineering workflows (agent tooling, MCP) and evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tooling &amp;amp; Process&lt;/strong&gt;: Proficiency with Jira/Confluence, Git-based workflows, and Agile/Scrum in cross-functional squads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Korea Office Benefits &amp;amp; Perks Offered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Point Reward Program for Customer Integration team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support 4 social insurance plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family leave (Maternity, Paternity)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid office work-arrangement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complimentary lunches, snacks and beverages during on-site working days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefit allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phone &amp;amp; Internet reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Accessory Allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English Support class&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual health checkup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holiday Appreciation Gift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;You will lead an engineering team responsible for in-vehicle middleware and platform services for the Sonatus Fastlane Collector and Copilot products, with a focus on people management, process, architecture, and code reviews.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity for an engineering leader who enjoys growing people, improving engineering systems and guiding technical direction in a complex embedded software environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We would encourage candidates with experience in other highly reliable embedded environments such as industrial automation, robotics, medical devices, telecommunications, aerospace or IoT to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, mentor, and grow an embedded software development team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster an inclusive, collaborative culture focused on technical excellence, continuous learning and ownership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the planning and delivery of software for Fastlane products on embedded Linux and High-Performance Compute (HPC) platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide architectural oversight through system design and code reviews, ensuring the software meets high-availability, low-latency, and fault-tolerance requirements for vehicle telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align agile development practices with automotive reliability standards (e.g., MISRA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) testing strategies and resolve integration bottlenecks in partnership with Hardware Engineering and QA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve developer workflows in collaboration with the internal tools team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate LLM/agentic tooling into the engineering environment to increase development velocity while maintaining code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree (BS, MS, or PhD) in Computer Science, Electrical/Computer Engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in embedded software development, including technical leadership and architectural design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of engineering management experience with direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to communicate complex development trade-offs clearly to Product, Hardware, and QA teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering commercial software products for mission-critical, internet-connected devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience building embedded systems, modern C++, inter-process communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded operating systems (Linux, Android, QNX) and HIL testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing communication protocols (CAN, Ethernet, HTTP, MQTT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with automotive standards (e.g., AUTOSAR Adaptive, UDS) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sonatus is looking for an experienced Senior Engineering Manager to build and lead our AI Validation function — the team responsible for how we test, evaluate, and govern the AI models and agentic capabilities embedded in our software-defined vehicle and cloud platforms, as well as our cloud-only AI and LLM-based products. You will deeply understand how AI is developed and deployed across Sonatus’s embedded, cloud, and LLM/RAG-driven environments, identify gaps and friction in current validation practices, and turn those insights into scalable test strategy, evaluation frameworks, and governance mechanisms that let Sonatus ship trustworthy AI-driven features at automotive scale. You will lead and grow a high-performing AI validation team and partner closely with engineering, product, and safety stakeholders to make AI quality and safety a competitive advantage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive Sonatus&#39;s AI validation strategy across embedded, in-vehicle, cloud-connected, and cloud-native AI systems, identifying gaps in model development, testing, deployment, and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, hire, mentor, and grow a high-performing AI Validation organization, establishing scalable engineering processes, technical direction, and execution excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end validation strategy for AI/ML models, LLMs, RAG pipelines, and agentic AI workflows—from data pipelines and model training through cloud services and in-vehicle deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and operationalize scalable evaluation frameworks and benchmarking platforms for AI systems, including multi-step agentic workflows, using deterministic metrics, LLM-as-a-Judge methodologies, automated regression testing, and production feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain evaluation harnesses for RAG and agentic systems that measure retrieval quality, grounding, citation accuracy, factual consistency, context relevance, safety, latency, reliability, and execution correctness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, integrate, and optimize open-source and commercial AI validation technologies, driving build-versus-buy decisions for Sonatus&#39;s AI quality platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish AI governance, Responsible AI practices, model lineage, safety guardrails, and compliance processes appropriate for automotive safety-critical systems and enterprise AI products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the quality gatekeeper for AI-enabled releases, partnering with engineering, product, safety, and OEM stakeholders to identify risks, define release criteria, and ensure production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across engineering teams to define validation strategies for emerging AI capabilities, rapidly prototype new evaluation approaches, and standardize successful practices into reusable frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement by tracking industry advances in AI evaluation, agentic AI, LLM validation, and RAG systems, translating them into scalable validation capabilities across Sonatus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field required (MS preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in software or systems engineering—including embedded, cloud, networking, security, or automotive domains—with 3+ years leading high-performing engineering or QA organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience developing, deploying, testing, or operating AI/ML systems, with strong expertise in modern ML workflows, neural networks, and MLOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of LLMs, RAG architectures, vector databases, embeddings, retrieval optimization, and agentic AI frameworks such as LangGraph or equivalent orchestration platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing and implementing scalable evaluation frameworks for AI systems, including multi-step agentic workflows, regression testing, benchmarking, and automated quality scoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise with hybrid evaluation methodologies combining deterministic validation (citation grounding, structural validation, exact matching) and probabilistic LLM-as-a-Judge techniques (faithfulness, answer relevance, context precision, task completion).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with RAG evaluation frameworks such as RAGAS, including evaluation tuning, embedding optimization, retrieval quality improvement, and production-scale LLM evaluation pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience validating hallucination, grounding, citation accuracy, bias, fairness, toxicity, and factual consistency in production LLM applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing systems that verify external knowledge claims and ensure responses are grounded in traceable citations and trusted data sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience testing cloud-native platforms and cloud-managed embedded products, including end-to-end system validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing AI governance, safety, compliance, and Responsible AI practices for enterprise or safety-critical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python, Linux, shell scripting, modern test frameworks (PyTest, Playwright, Behave), and engineering productivity tools such as Jenkins and JIRA.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways to Stand Out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience validating AI or agentic systems in safety-critical or regulated industries (automotive, aerospace, medical).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record building and scaling an AI test/evaluation platform or developer experience used by multiple teams (frameworks, reusable components, reference implementations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated wins moving AI testing practices from ad hoc to standardized, organization-wide adoption, with measurable impact on cycle time, quality, or reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing enterprise-grade AI governance (auditability, monitoring, policy enforcement) in production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience evaluating LLM and RAG systems at scale, including agentic workflows, RAGAS-based evaluation, citation verification, hallucination detection, groundedness, faithfulness, answer relevance, tool/task correctness, and automated regression testing across offline and online feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sunnyvale HQ Benefits &amp;amp; Perks Offered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health care plan (Medical, Dental &amp;amp; Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and Dependent Care Expense program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement plan (401k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Insurance (Basic, Voluntary &amp;amp; AD&amp;amp;D)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid time off per year, 14+ paid holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid office work arrangement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complimentary lunches, snacks, and beverages during on-site working days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefit allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phone &amp;amp; Internet reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Accessory Allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The posted salary range is a general guideline and represents a good faith estimate of what Sonatus (&quot;Company&quot;) could reasonably expect to pay for a base salary for this position. The pay offered to a selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, geographic location and external market pay for comparable jobs. The Company reserves the right to modify this range in the future, as needed, as market conditions change.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$240,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$290,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Embedded Software Engineer to develop and optimise our core in-vehicle software platform for Sonatus Fastlane Collector and Copilot products. In this role, you will be a key contributor to next-generation vehicle applications, middleware, and platform services running on automotive-grade High-Performance Compute (HPC) platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and optimize high-performance in-vehicle applications and connectivity middleware, ensuring low latency and high-throughput data transfer between vehicles and the cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and support robust platform services responsible for system-wide resource management, health monitoring, and lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and root-cause issues across development, testing, and production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author comprehensive unit and integration tests. Conduct code reviews to maintain high standards of code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to established development processes and create clear design documents to facilitate design reviews and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional software development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, maths, physics, or a similar field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in modern C++ (C++14/17), with a deep understanding of RAII, smart pointers, multithreading, inter-process communication, and memory management in resource-constrained environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience developing, cross-compiling, testing, and debugging on Embedded Linux. Experience with Android, QNX, and other POSIX-compliant operating systems is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing automated unit and integration tests using modern C++ testing frameworks and Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern transport protocols (HTTP, MQTT) and serialization formats (Protobuf, FlatBuffers, JSON).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to vehicle network/diagnostic standards (CAN, Ethernet, SOME/IP, UDS) or automotive industry standards such as Adaptive AUTOSAR is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Rust is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player with excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;At Sonatus, we’re driving the transformation to AI-enabled software-defined vehicles. Traditional automotive software methods can’t keep pace with consumer expectations shaped by the mobile industry—where features evolve rapidly, update seamlessly, and improve continuously. That’s why leading OEMs trust Sonatus to accelerate this shift. Our technology is already in production across more than 9 million vehicles on the road today and rapidly expanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #444444;&quot;&gt;Headquartered in Sunnyvale, CA, with 250+ employees worldwide, Sonatus combines the agility of a fast-growing company with the scale and impact of an established partner. Backed by strong funding and proven by global deployment, we’re solving some of the most interesting and complex challenges in the industry. Join us and help redefine what’s possible as we shape the future of mobility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sonatus, we are redefining the future of Software-Defined Vehicles (SDV) through agility and innovation. To achieve this, we operate as &lt;strong&gt;Mission-Driven Squads&lt;/strong&gt;, where each team takes &lt;strong&gt;full end-to-end ownership&lt;/strong&gt; of a specific module to deliver production-ready software with speed and precision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer - Customer Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to join one of our squads (e.g., Secure Network, Data Hub) as a core member. In this role, you will go beyond traditional coding; you will act as a &lt;strong&gt;Full-Cycle Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; who ensures the quality and reliability of the features you build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is ideal for an experienced C/C++ developer who is passionate about delivering excellence. By leveraging AI tools like GitHub Copilot and Claude, you will drive the entire engineering lifecycle—&lt;strong&gt;from implementation to verification&lt;/strong&gt;—safeguarding the integrity of our software for millions of vehicles on the road.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Squad Mission Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work under the guidance of the Squad Lead to execute the full engineering lifecycle—from &lt;strong&gt;Implementation&lt;/strong&gt; to &lt;strong&gt;Verification&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switch roles flexibly based on the squad’s goals (e.g., focusing on feature development in one sprint, and shifting to verification tasks in the next) to ensure the mission is accomplished.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Cross-Functional Engineering (Hybrid Dev &amp;amp; QA)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and develop high-quality C/C++ embedded software based on customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verification:&lt;/strong&gt; Design Python-based test cases and build automation frameworks to verify both your own code and the squad’s deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Treat documentation as code. Create and maintain detailed technical documentation—including APIs, dependencies, and integration guides—to ensure the software is accessible, maintainable, and seamlessly integrated by customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Review:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in Code Reviews not just for logic, but with a focus on Testability and Safety, ensuring the code is robust before it merges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Quality Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a culture of total ownership. You define &quot;Done&quot; not merely by implementation, but by delivering software that is Production-Ready and rigorously validated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively troubleshoot and resolve build/test failures in the CI/CD pipeline as if they were your own code errors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. AI-Augmented Workflow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools such as GitHub Copilot and Claude to maximize productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI to lower the barrier for cross-functional tasks (e.g., generating test scenarios for complex logic, or debugging unfamiliar code), allowing you to focus on high-value engineering challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Customer Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-site Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Support major test events with partners on-site (domestic/international), troubleshooting integration issues directly in vehicle or test bench environments to ensure successful deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a primary technical contact for integration issues, translating complex engineering concepts into clear guidance for customer engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Foundation: Development Skills]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 6+ years of experience in embedded software development or engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Language&lt;/strong&gt;: Proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;C/C++&lt;/strong&gt; programming (strong understanding of pointers, memory management, and data structures).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OS Environment&lt;/strong&gt;: Solid experience in development and debugging within a &lt;strong&gt;Linux&lt;/strong&gt; environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Key Differentiator: QA Capability &amp;amp; Mindset]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scripting&lt;/strong&gt;: Experience using &lt;strong&gt;Python &lt;/strong&gt;for writing test scripts or automating engineering tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing Willingness&lt;/strong&gt;: A flexible attitude with a strong belief that &quot;&lt;strong&gt;Testing is Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;.&quot; You are willing to balance your time between Dev and QA tasks (even up to 50:50) depending on the squad&#39;s needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Critical Thinking&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to look beyond the &quot;Happy Path&quot; and critically ask, &lt;em&gt;&quot;Is this truly safe for the user?&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Knowledge and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Automotive Standards &amp;amp; Quality]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards &amp;amp; Audit:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience in automotive design reviews and audit processes based on standards such as &lt;strong&gt;ISO 26262 (Functional Safety)&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Automotive SPICE (ASPICE)&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;ASIL&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Quality Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience adhering to &lt;strong&gt;MISRA C/C++&lt;/strong&gt; coding standards and using static analysis tools such as &lt;strong&gt;Coverity&lt;/strong&gt;, Polyspace, or similar products to manage code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[Collaboration &amp;amp; Tools]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working in Cross-functional Squads or Agile/Scrum environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency with Jira/Confluence and Git-based workflows (Branching, Pull Requests).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frameworks:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with Unit/Integration test frameworks (e.g., PyTest, GoogleTest).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network Protocols:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of automotive communication protocols (Ethernet, CAN, SOME/IP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Eagerness to learn and adopt new technologies and AI tools to enhance workflow efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
